prompt:
You are the director of a {{videoType}} video about "{{topic}}" in {{language}}. The script is already written. Your job is ONLY to direct how it looks and moves: for each scene decide what it is for, how it communicates visually, and how it is shot. Do NOT rewrite any narration. Return ONLY valid JSON without markdown formatting.

Video plan:
- Visual look shared by every scene: {{visualPalette}}
- Vocal tone: {{voiceTone}}
- Image budget: at most {{maxImages}} scene(s) in this batch may use a generated image

Scenes (JSON). Each lists its neighbours ("previous" / "next" titles) and its beat - use them so adjacent scenes look different and the pictures follow the story:
{{sceneDigest}}

Rules:
- Return exactly one entry per scene listed, using the same sceneNumber
- "purpose" is what the scene is FOR in the story, one of: hook, introduction, explanation, example, comparison, data, quote, summary, conclusion, cta, transition
- "strategy" is how the scene communicates, one of: title, text, list, timeline, quote, statistics, comparison, split-visual, visual-explanation, full-screen-visual. Choose by what the scene actually says: ordered steps -> timeline; parallel points -> list; exactly two things compared -> comparison; one striking number -> statistics; one memorable sentence -> quote; prose -> text
- "layout" is one of: title-only, stack-list, grid, timeline, paragraph-stack, quote-feature, stat-highlight, comparison-split, split-image, image-fullbleed - or "" to let the system decide. A step-by-step process -> timeline; four or more parallel points -> grid; exactly two things compared -> comparison-split; one striking number or statistic -> stat-highlight; one memorable sentence -> quote-feature. Use split-image or image-fullbleed only when visual.kind is "image". Vary the layout from the neighbouring scenes: never use the same layout in three scenes in a row, and prefer a different one from "previous" when the content allows
- "visual.kind" is "image" only when a picture adds meaning the narration alone does not (a concrete object, place, scene or metaphor). Most scenes should be "none". Never use an image for scenes that are mostly numbers or lists
- "visual.prompt" is, when kind is "image", one concrete image description in English written for THIS scene: its subject, setting, lighting and style, 15-40 words, consistent with the shared visual look and with the story around it (look at "previous" and "next"). No text, letters, logos, charts or screenshots inside the image. Leave it "" when kind is "none"
- "cameraMotion" is one of: static, zoom-in, zoom-out, pan-left, pan-right. Slow zoom-in for emphasis, a pan for scenes with an image, static for dense text. Do not use a camera move in every scene
- "transition" is one of: fade, slide, slideUp, wipe, irisWipe, zoom, cut. Prefer fade inside a beat; use a slide or wipe when the beat changes; use cut only for a deliberate jolt

Required JSON format:
{
  "scenes": [
    { "sceneNumber": 1, "purpose": "hook", "strategy": "text", "layout": "", "visual": { "kind": "none", "prompt": "" }, "cameraMotion": "static", "transition": "fade" }
  ]
}
